  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 103 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nRidging moves back east over the area Friday into the weekend. This \nwill help suppress most convection once again outside of maybe an \nisolated storm in the mountains. Temperatures will climb back up a \nfew degrees, but it's possible much of the region will stay below \n100. Model solutions diverge later next week as they struggle with \nthe strength and placement of the upper ridge. Fall is just around \nthe corner as September begins so a pattern change to \nwetter/cooler becomes more likely in the coming weeks (we hope!).",
